    <tok fileIndex="0" linenr="24" column="1" str="/*x  A brief summary of the date string formats this parser groks:xx  RFC 2616 3.3.1xx  Sun, 06 Nov 1994 08:49:37 GMT  ; RFC 822, updated by RFC 1123x  Sunday, 06-Nov-94 08:49:37 GMT ; RFC 850, obsoleted by RFC 1036x  Sun Nov  6 08:49:37 1994       ; ANSI C&apos;s asctime() formatxx  we support dates without week day name:xx  06 Nov 1994 08:49:37 GMTx  06-Nov-94 08:49:37 GMTx  Nov  6 08:49:37 1994xx  without the time zone:xx  06 Nov 1994 08:49:37x  06-Nov-94 08:49:37xx  weird order:xx  1994 Nov 6 08:49:37  (GNU date fails)x  GMT 08:49:37 06-Nov-94 Sundayx  94 6 Nov 08:49:37    (GNU date fails)xx  time left out:xx  1994 Nov 6x  06-Nov-94x  Sun Nov 6 94xx  unusual separators:xx  1994.Nov.6x  Sun/Nov/6/94/GMTxx  commonly used time zone names:xx  Sun, 06 Nov 1994 08:49:37 CETx  06 Nov 1994 08:49:37 ESTxx  time zones specified using RFC822 style:xx  Sun, 12 Sep 2004 15:05:58 -0700x  Sat, 11 Sep 2004 21:32:11 +0200xx  compact numerical date strings:xx  20040912 15:05:58 -0700x  20040911 +0200xx*/"/>
